<c74object name='evi_freezeverbtrigger' module='gen-evi' category='evieve'> <!-- kind='genobject_dsp'> -->
    <digest>
        evieve Gen Object. Classic freeverb reverb algorithm with buttery smooth freezing effect controllable at audio rate <br />
    </digest>
    <description>
        <b>evi_freezeverbtrigger</b> is an abstraction for using inside <o>gen~</o> or <b>GenExpr</b>. <br />
         <br />
        evi_freezeverbtrigger.gendsp requires the GenExpr file(s): <br />
        <o>evi_reverb_library</o>.genexpr <br />
         <br />
	    This is a basic Schroeder reverb effect but with additional filtering and controls. The main feature here is the ability to smoothly capture the input audio in the recirculating feedback path in a way which gives a forever freezing effect. This can be triggered and released with wet+dry or with wet alone. In the <o>evi.freezeverb~</o>) abstraction, which wraps the <o>evi_freezeverb</o> gen~ abstraction, this freezing effect is achieved at message rate. The point of this <o>evi_freezeverbtrigger</o> abstraction is to offer the freeze and retrigger functions as audio-rate inlets so that triggering the effect can be done in audio only control rate processing scenarios. <br />
    </description>
    <methodlist />
    <constructorlist>
        <constructor name='1'>
            <digest>
                { arguments={}, inlets={ left, right, freeze, retrigger } }
            </digest>
        </constructor>
    </constructorlist>
    <geninletlist>
        <geninlet name='left' type='float' optional='1'>
            <digest>
                Signal Input. Audio input left.
            </digest>
        </geninlet>
        <geninlet name='right' type='float' optional='1'>
            <digest>
                Signal Input. Audio input right.
            </digest>
        </geninlet>
        <geninlet name='freeze' type='float' optional='1'>
            <digest>
                0/1/2 @default 0. Audio rate or message rate control of freezing effect; 0&#x3D;off, 1&#x3D;on+dry, 2&#x3D;on-wet-only.
            </digest>
        </geninlet>
        <geninlet name='retrigger' type='float' optional='1'>
            <digest>
                Freeze. Audio rate sync signal to &#x27;retrigger&#x27; the current freeze effect.
            </digest>
        </geninlet>
    </geninletlist>
